{"root":"pli/ms","translators":["sujato"],"title":"Poets","html":"<article id='an4.231'><header><ul><li class='division'><span class='root'>Aṅguttara Nikāya 4.231 </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>Numbered Discourses 4.231 </span></li>\n<li><span class='root'>23. Duccaritavagga </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>23. Bad Conduct </span></li></ul>\n<h1 class='sutta-title'><span class='root'>Kavisutta </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>Poets </span></h1></header>\n<p><span class='root'>“Cattārome, bhikkhave, kavī. </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>“Mendicants, there are these four poets. </span>\n<span class='root'>Katame cattāro? </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>What four? </span></p>\n<p><span class='root'>Cintākavi, sutakavi, atthakavi, paṭibhānakavi—</span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>A poet who thoughtfully composes their own work, a poet who repeats the oral transmission, a poet who educates, and a poet who improvises. </span></p>\n<p><span class='root'>Ime kho, bhikkhave, cattāro kavī”ti. </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>These are the four poets.” </span></p>\n<p class='endsutta'><span class='root'>Ekādasamaṁ. </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'></span></p>\n<p class='endvagga'><span class='root'>Duccaritavaggo tatiyo. </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'></span></p>\n<p class='uddana-intro'><span class='root'>Tassuddānaṁ </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'></span></p>\n<blockquote class='uddanagatha'><p><span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>Duccaritaṁ diṭṭhi akataññū ca, </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'></span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>Pāṇātipātāpi dve maggā; </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'></span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>Dve vohārapathā vuttā, </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'></span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>Ahirikaṁ duppaññakavinā cāti. </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'></span></span></p></blockquote></article>"}
